# LOOP
brief → execute (sub-agent) → verify (YOU run the DoD-slice) → fix → repeat, then ONE
simplify pass (code-simplifier over the wave's integrated diff) → re-verify. Max 5
rounds. Escalation ladder: the executor's 2nd failure of the SAME DoD line moves the
task one tier up as a NEW agent carrying the attempt log ({{sonnet → opus → you |
opus → you on ⚠gate waves}}); 3 attempts on the SAME failure at session level
without converging → stop and report (don't degrade tests, don't mark done what
isn't done). The simplify pass consumes NO round: if the FULL DoD-auto fails after it,
ONE fix round to the SAME simplifier (SendMessage, cost 0); a second failure → revert
to the checkpoint commit and close on the pre-simplify diff, logged. Duplication an
executor reports that this SCOPE does not name: if EVERY implicated file is already in
this wave's SCOPE, amend the brief(s) and extract in-wave (helper first, consumers
after, serialized) and update the card at close; if ANY file is outside, log it in the
`Reuse:` follow-up field and refresh the later-wave manifests at doc-sync. Never
improvise. {{Wave-specific failure policy: known flaky checks, retries that don't
count as failures, when to stop early and leave DoD-human.}}

# VISUAL CHECK (mandatory if the wave touches UI: .pug/.html/.scss/.css/components)
grep + build only prove the code is THERE, not that it LOOKS right — they never catch real width,
wrong-language text, or overflow/overlap. Before marking a UI task completed, DELEGATE the capture to a
`sonnet` sub-agent (1 of the 20, 0 Opus quota; the main session does not render or screenshot) that renders the
page in headless Chrome and RETURNS the PNG paths plus its findings:
- It renders against a local server (full env) or, if it can't boot, the deployed URL.
- It screenshots with a headless-Chrome helper (Playwright/Puppeteer + the system browser, e.g.
  `node {{repo}}/scripts/shot.{{cjs|mjs — match the repo's module system}} <url> <out.png> [lang] [width]`). Capture desktop (≥1280) AND mobile (375);
  both languages if the app is i18n. {{If the project has no screenshot helper, the FIRST UI task creates one.}}
- It checks width/responsive (not "compacted"), i18n correct, no overlaps, design-system
  fonts/colors and reports each finding. You (the orchestrator) MAY open those PNGs to judge —
  reviewing sub-agent output is allowed. Only then mark the UI task completed; the courier later sends
  those same PNGs as media.

# WORKFLOW (fan-out)
AGENT BUDGET & ROLES: max 20 sub-agents in this session TOTAL, one counter starting
at zero, `model` always explicit. YOU (the main session) ORCHESTRATE: you decide
design and scope, audit what investigators DELIVER (solution · files ·
considerations · open questions — never code) against this SCOPE, write one
executor brief per task, run every DoD-slice and the full DoD-auto YOURSELF, and
integrate. You do NOT implement first, and you never audit a diff with a sub-agent
of your own tier. `opus` sub-agents investigate, review regression and verify (quota
10, 2 reserved: the ⚠gate verifier and the simplify pass; audits pass to `sonnet`
once the rest is spent).
`sonnet` sub-agents IMPLEMENT NO-gate tasks from your briefs — ≤4 in parallel with
EXCLUSIVE ownership of disjoint files, each in its own worktree; a shared helper is
NOT a disjoint file, so the task extracting it closes before its consumers start and
never runs beside them — and return diff
summary + DoD-slice commands with output + what they extracted or consumed + doubts,
never a bare "done". ONE simplify pass per wave: the packaged agent
`code-simplifier:code-simplifier` called with an explicit `model: {{opus | the auditor tier of this session when the main session is not Fable}}` and the
`## Simplifier brief` below — it costs 1 of the 20 and 1 of the Opus quota, it EDITS
code so it never self-approves (YOU re-run the FULL DoD-auto after it), and on ⚠gate
waves it runs BEFORE the reserved verifier. At close one delivery `courier` per batch
(`adcm-toolkits:artifact-courier`; normally 1, each extra batch = 1 more of the 20) is spawned with
`model: sonnet` ALWAYS — even under Fable —, 0 of the Opus quota (see GUARDRAILS & CLOSE).
Follow-ups to a live agent (SendMessage) cost 0; a new agent costs 1. In ultracode: Workflow
scripts per phase (investigate → implement → review) with ≤20 agent() calls in
total, `isolation: 'worktree'` on parallel executors, no unbounded loops or panels.
The 21st agent is a protocol violation — stop and ask. Log `agents used: n/20 (opus
a · sonnet b) · escalations` at close. You are a PURE orchestrator
(`references/orchestrator-rule.md` of the skill `execution-prompt-architect`): you do
not read files in bulk, edit at scale, render, browse or publish — only the ≤~20-line
logged fixes — and every `Agent`/`Workflow` call, Plan and Explore agents included,
names its `model`. The user's `sin tanto lío` (that task) or `modo directo` (until
`modo orquestador`) switches it off.
